{
  "dependencyId": "sfx-identity-login",
  "meaning": "Sign-in against sfx-identity, declared so the estate signs a caller in with no login host of its own. open-session begins the attempt (the throttle, the principal and its verifier: sfx-identity begin_api_login), derives the Argon2id tag of the password with Konscious.Security.Cryptography.Argon2 1.3.1 and Blake2 1.1.1 (the libraries the former login host ran, downloaded from nuget.org and loaded only when each package has its declared SHA-256), compares it with the verifier, mints a 32-byte bearer and completes the attempt with the match and the bearer SHA-256 (complete_api_login). The password, the verifier and the bearer meet only inside this one program; sfx-identity receives the realm, identifier and source, then the attempt, the match and the bearer hash. derive-tag derives the Argon2id tag of a password and salt under the same parameters.",
  "objectGraphClosure": "object-graph.v1",
